I accepted the RNAfold minimum free energy (MFE) structure as returned, at −28.5 kcal/mol. It is a computational prediction only: I did not change any pairs, add pseudoknots, or check it against comparative or experimental data. I counted the string and it is exactly 173 characters.

**Overall shape:**
- **Long-range helix:** a 6-bp helix pairs positions 3–8 with 142–147. It encloses a multibranch region with six inner stem-loops.
- **Inner stem-loops:** these include
  - a short hairpin at 10–19;
  - a 7-bp hairpin at 23–39;
  - a three-part helix with an internal loop spanning 40–74;
  - a two-part stem-loop at 77–101;
  - a branched domain at 105–141.
- **3′ hairpin:** a separate stem-loop sits at 148–170, followed by three unpaired 3′ nucleotides.

